<Style id="s-landmark"><IconStyle><color>ff545f67</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Style id="s-practical"><IconStyle><color>ff818c95</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Folder><name>Venue</name>
<Placemark><name>Riverside Theater</name><styleUrl>#s-venue</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The Riverside is a 1928 French Baroque vaudeville palace on the west bank of the Milwaukee River, and Widespread Panic&#x27;s unofficial Midwest home. I have only seen it in photographs, and in every one the balcony looks like it is leaning over the stage.<br>116 W Wisconsin Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br><a href="https://www.pabsttheatergroup.com/venues/riverside-theater">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Riverside+Theater+116+W+Wisconsin+Ave+Milwaukee+WI+53203">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9109,43.039,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Hotel</name>
<Placemark><name>Drury Plaza Hotel Milwaukee Downtown</name><styleUrl>#s-hotel</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The Drury sits inside the 1928 Art Deco First Financial Centre at Water and Wisconsin, directly across the river from the Riverside. The free 5:30 Kickback (hot appetizers and drinks) lines up with pre-show, and the free hot breakfast will do its part the morning after.<br>700 N Water St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://www.druryhotels.com/locations/milwaukee-wi/drury-plaza-hotel-milwaukee-downtown">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Drury+Plaza+Hotel+Milwaukee+Downtown+700+N+Water+St+Milwaukee+WI+53202">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9088,43.0389,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Watch the game</name>
<Placemark><name>The Deer Garden at Deer District</name><styleUrl>#s-watch-party</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The city&#x27;s official free outdoor watch party: a big screen in the Deer Garden plaza outside Fiserv Forum, ringed by bars and restaurants running Brewers promotions. Friday the Bucks open their season against the Bulls at 3 PM in the arena next door, so the plaza will be humming by mid-afternoon. This is where Milwaukee goes to lose its mind together.<br>1134 N Vel R. Phillips Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br>Hours: Plaza is open all day; watch party programming begins with the Bucks game at 3 PM Friday, Brewers first pitch 7 PM. Saturday implied but not explicitly confirmed (see open_questions). Dress warm; late October nights in Milwaukee run 35-45 F.<br><a href="https://deerdistrict.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=The+Deer+Garden+at+Deer+District+Milwaukee&amp;query_place_id=ChIJPZ9zGyMZBYgRmNoONk8FinQ">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9159,43.045,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tom&#x27;s Watch Bar</name><styleUrl>#s-watch-party</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The most screens in the city, all with the sound up, in a 360-degree stadium-seating room on the Deer District plaza. They have committed to every Brewers postseason game, take reservations for playoff tables (it fills), and the food runs a notch above wings-and-fries. I have not sat in it. Reviewers who have say it is the ballpark without the $2,900 ticket.<br>1134 N Vel R. Phillips Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br>Hours: Fri 11:00 AM-12:00 AM; Sat 10:00 AM-12:00 AM; Sun 11:00 AM-12:00 AM; Mon 4:00 PM-12:00 AM. Bucks pregame party Fri 1 PM, UFC watch Sat 1 PM, Packers watch Sun 3:25 PM.<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/toms-watch-bar-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://tomswatchbar.com/milwaukee/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Tom%27s+Watch+Bar+Milwaukee&amp;query_place_id=ChIJEbbO0v4ZBYgRjEE3UnbLF_c">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9156,43.0452,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Major Goolsby&#x27;s</name><styleUrl>#s-watch-party</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Milwaukee&#x27;s old-school sports bar, two blocks from the Riverside, walls covered in signed memorabilia and TVs everywhere. $10 pitchers during every World Series game, giant pretzels, wings, burgers. The closest place to catch first pitch and still make the opening notes of set 1.<br>340 W Kilbourn Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br>Hours: Fri 11:00 AM-11:00 PM; Sat 11:00 AM-11:00 PM; Sun 11:00 AM-9:00 PM; Mon 4:00-9:00 PM. $10 beer pitchers during every World Series game.<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/major-goolsbys-milwaukee-2?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.majorgoolsbys.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Major+Goolsby%27s+Milwaukee&amp;query_place_id=ChIJ3VkbA3UZBYgRC3Z4Ai_xQew">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9156,43.0417,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Third Ward World Series Block Party (Catalano Square)</name><styleUrl>#s-watch-party</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A two-day free street party in the prettiest neighborhood downtown: Menomonee St closed to cars, giant video screens in Catalano Square, food trucks, Brewers-themed cocktails from the Third Ward Beer Garden, and live tapings of the Foul Territory podcast (Corey Knebel, Kevin Pillar, Alanna Rizzo) 5-7 PM both days. FOX One&#x27;s &#x27;Relive Live&#x27; pop-up is a mock 1980s living room full of Brewers memorabilia and bobbleheads, noon-4 PM. Friday they are giving away two Game 1 tickets plus a shuttle (enter noon-5:15 PM).<br>147 N Broadway, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri Oct 23 and Sat Oct 24, noon-11:00 PM both days. Foul Territory live 5-7 PM; FOX One pop-up noon-4 PM; Bill Michaels Show live 10 AM-2 PM. Closed Sunday/Monday.<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/third-ward-beer-garden-at-catalano-square-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://historicthirdward.org/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Third+Ward+World+Series+Block+Party+%28Catalano+Square%29+Milwaukee&amp;query_place_id=ChIJo7PvSp4ZBYgR8Q87Bh_WV_A">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9067,43.0313,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cafe Benelux</name><styleUrl>#s-watch-party</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Lowlands Group&#x27;s Belgian-style grand cafe with a rooftop patio in the heart of the Third Ward, two blocks from the block party. Official watch parties with buy-one-get-one Lowlands Brewing Collaborative beers from 5 PM, and they have promised to stay open until the final out. Frites and mussels instead of wings. This one is on reputation, and the reputation is sit-down and grown-up.<br>346 N Broadway, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri 7:00 AM-12:00 AM; Sat 7:00 AM-12:00 AM; Sun 7:00 AM-11:00 PM; Mon 7:00 AM-11:00 PM. BOGO Lowlands beers from 5 PM on game days; open until the game ends.<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/caf%C3%A9-benelux-milwaukee-2?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.cafebenelux.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Cafe+Benelux+Milwaukee&amp;query_place_id=ChIJZ_10J6QZBYgRjajwdJ3ukeg">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9071,43.0349,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>90s2K Cafe</name><styleUrl>#s-watch-party</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A nostalgia bar (90s and 2000s decor, DJs, big dance floor) a block from the Deer District, throwing a &#x27;1982 Retro Watch Party&#x27; Friday and Saturday for the last time the Brewers were in the World Series. Doors 5 PM, 82-cent taps from 6-7 PM, Brewers gear required for the specials. Loud and young, and a Panic fan would enjoy the pregame.<br>1103 N Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Dr, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br>Hours: Watch party Fri Oct 23 and Sat Oct 24: doors 5:00 PM, 82-cent taps 6:00-7:00 PM, open until 2:30 AM. Posted regular hours: Fri 7 PM-2:30 AM, Sat 4 PM-2:30 AM, Sun 4 PM-2 AM, Mon closed.<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=90s2K+Cafe+Milwaukee&amp;query_place_id=ChIJlfXJIQAZBYgR0G97snf2PhE">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9146,43.0445,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Who&#x27;s on Third</name><styleUrl>#s-watch-party</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The Brewers bar downtown: wings, brats, an outdoor patio, and a game-day shuttle to American Family Field that reviewers come back for on consecutive game days. Four blocks from the Riverside on the walk toward the Deer District. Open until 2:30 AM Friday and Saturday, so it works as a post-show stop for highlights and the mood. Never been inside, but a Brewers bar on a World Series night does not need my review.<br>1007 N Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Dr (Old World Third St), Milwaukee, WI 53203<br>Hours: Fri 11:00 AM-2:30 AM; Sat 11:00 AM-2:30 AM; Sun 11:00 AM-2:00 AM; Mon 11:00 AM-2:00 AM (Google listing). No World Series-specific promo confirmed.<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/whos-on-third-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Who%27s+on+Third+Milwaukee&amp;query_place_id=ChIJC4Uvv3QZBYgRElnmPP7d1no">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9146,43.0432,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Central Waters Brewing Co. Milwaukee Taproom</name><styleUrl>#s-watch-party</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A craft brewery taproom inside a converted 1880s church in the old Pabst brewery district, about a 15-minute walk west of the Deer District. The game goes on a projector with audio through the whole bar. World Series specials are $1 off full pours, $4 tallboys of Grand Slam Lager, and 8 bone-in wings with fries for $14, and Trouble Makers Cocina serves Mexican food on site. The calmest option of the watch spots, and the best beer.<br>1037 W Juneau Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53233<br>Hours: Fri 11:00 AM-10:00 PM; Sat 11:00 AM-10:00 PM; Sun 11:00 AM-7:00 PM; Mon 3:00-9:00 PM (posted). Specials run all day on World Series game days; unconfirmed whether they stay open past 10 PM to the final out.<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/central-waters-brewing-milwaukee-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://centralwaters.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Central+Waters+Brewing+Co.+Milwaukee+Taproom+Milwaukee&amp;query_place_id=ChIJC5y5gqgZBYgRiVsH67MVAyk">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9255,43.0456,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Live music</name>
<Placemark><name>Street Party Stage, W Wisconsin Ave at the Riverside Theater</name><styleUrl>#s-stage</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The city shuts this one block of Wisconsin Avenue, bridge included, to cars from Friday noon through Sunday night, and Pabst Theater Group turns it into a free outdoor pre-party. Wolph plays at 5:30 PM each day, so the hotel, a beer on the pavement and the Riverside doors at 6:30 PM line up in one straight walk.<br>W Wisconsin Ave between N Plankinton Ave and N Water St (in front of the Riverside Theater, 116 W Wisconsin Ave), Milwaukee, WI 53203<br><a href="https://www.pabsttheatergroup.com/events/detail/wolph">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Riverside+Theater+116+W+Wisconsin+Ave+Milwaukee+WI">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9108,43.0388,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Wolph: Free Street Party Before Widespread Panic</name><styleUrl>#s-stage</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Pabst Theater Group&#x27;s free outdoor pre-party on Wisconsin Avenue right outside the Riverside, all three nights. Wolph is a young Grateful Dead-leaning jam band whose originals are being produced by Panic&#x27;s own Dave Schools, so the lot is a family affair. Doors 12:00 PM, music 5:30 PM, then straight into the theater at 6:30.<br>W Wisconsin Ave outside the Riverside Theater, 116 W Wisconsin Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br><a href="https://www.pabsttheatergroup.com/events/detail/wolph">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Riverside+Theater+116+W+Wisconsin+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9109,43.0389,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Official Widespread Panic After-Parties at Mo&#x27;s Irish Pub</name><styleUrl>#s-stage</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Half a block west of the Riverside doors. Houseplant plays Friday and Saturday, Madison jamgrass quartet Armchair Boogie plays Sunday. Listed as 21+, starting 11:45 PM, which is the minute the Riverside lets out. This is the room where the whole run ends up.<br>142 W Wisconsin Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br><a href="https://www.pabsttheatergroup.com/events/detail/widespread-panic-2026">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Mo%27s+Irish+Pub+142+W+Wisconsin+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9116,43.0389,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Drink</name>
<Placemark><name>Mo&#x27;s Irish Pub</name><styleUrl>#s-bar</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Mo&#x27;s is the Irish pub next door to the Riverside marquee, at the west edge of the closed block. It is the official Widespread Panic after-party bar all three nights (Houseplant Fri/Sat, Armchair Boogie Sun, 21+, doors 11 PM) and the indoor fallback if the street gets cold.<br>142 W Wisconsin Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br>Hours: Fri 11:00 AM - late (site lists midnight in one place and 2:00 AM in another; the after-party runs past midnight) · Sat 11:00 AM - late (same caveat) · Mon 3:00 PM - 1:00 AM<br><a href="https://www.mosirishpub.com/milwaukee">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Mo%27s+Irish+Pub+142+W+Wisconsin+Ave+Milwaukee+WI">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9116,43.0389,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>SafeHouse</name><styleUrl>#s-bar</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A spy-themed bar hidden behind an unmarked red door on a side street, open since 1966. Entry takes a password, and without it &#x27;Agent Moneypenny&#x27; runs a clearance test while the whole bar watches on camera. Committed kitsch, a 4-minute walk from the Riverside, and I know it only by reputation, which is sixty years long.<br>779 N Front St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri 11:00 AM - 12:00 AM (kitchen to 10 PM) · Sat 11:00 AM - 12:00 AM (kitchen to 10 PM) · Sun 11:00 AM - 8:00 PM · Mon 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/safehouse-milwaukee">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.safe-house.com/milwaukee-restaurant">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=SafeHouse+779+N+Front+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9103,43.0406,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Blu at The Pfister Hotel</name><styleUrl>#s-bar</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Twenty-three floors above the city in the 1893 Pfister, with floor-to-ceiling views of downtown and Lake Michigan. Martinis, a deep wine list, live piano or jazz Friday and Saturday from 8 PM. Open until 2 AM Fri and Sat, which makes it the classiest nightcap after the show, a straight 8-minute walk east on Wisconsin Avenue.<br>424 E Wisconsin Ave, 23rd Floor, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri 4:00 PM - 2:00 AM (live music 8 PM - midnight) · Sat 4:00 PM - 2:00 AM (live music 8 PM - midnight) · Sun 5:00 PM - 12:00 AM · Mon 5:00 PM - 12:00 AM<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/blu-milwaukee">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.thepfisterhotel.com/dining/blu">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Blu+Pfister+Hotel+424+E+Wisconsin+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9057,43.0394,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mader&#x27;s Knight&#x27;s Bar</name><styleUrl>#s-bar</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The bar inside Milwaukee&#x27;s most famous German restaurant (since 1902), guarded by two suits of armor in the window and hung with medieval weaponry. A boot of German lager here before the show is the most Milwaukee thing within a 10-minute walk of the theater.<br>1041 N Old World 3rd St (now signed N Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Dr), Milwaukee, WI 53203<br>Hours: Fri 11:30 AM - 10:00 PM · Sat 11:30 AM - 10:00 PM · Sun 11:30 AM - 8:00 PM · Mon 11:30 AM - 9:00 PM<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/maders-restaurant-milwaukee">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.madersrestaurant.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Mader%27s+Restaurant+1041+N+Old+World+3rd+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9149,43.0439,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bryant&#x27;s Cocktail Lounge</name><styleUrl>#s-bar</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Milwaukee&#x27;s oldest cocktail lounge (1938) and one of the great bars in America: no menu, no visible bottles, just velvet, low light and a bartender who asks what you like and builds something from a house repertoire of hundreds of drinks. Open until 2 AM Friday and Saturday, a 10-minute rideshare south of the Riverside. I have not sat at that bar. I have read enough people who have to trust the velvet.<br>1579 S 9th St, Milwaukee, WI 53204<br>Hours: Fri 5:00 PM - 2:00 AM · Sat 3:00 PM - 2:00 AM · Sun 5:00 PM - 12:00 AM · Mon Closed<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/bryants-cocktail-lounge-milwaukee">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://bryantscocktaillounge.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Bryant%27s+Cocktail+Lounge+1579+S+9th+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9229,43.0144,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>At Random</name><styleUrl>#s-bar</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A 1964 Bay View time capsule of Naugahyde booths, swag lamps and ice-cream cocktails, saved and run by the same owner as Bryant&#x27;s. A Grasshopper or a Brandy Alexander the size of your head, in a room that looks like a Wes Anderson set. Fri/Sat open until 2 AM.<br>2501 S Delaware Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53207<br>Hours: Fri 5:00 PM - 2:00 AM · Sat 3:00 PM - 2:00 AM · Sun 3:00 PM - 12:00 AM · Mon Closed<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/at-random-milwaukee">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.atrandommke.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=At+Random+2501+S+Delaware+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.8914,42.9979,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Lost Whale</name><styleUrl>#s-bar</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Bay View&#x27;s best modern cocktail bar: tropical-leaning, sustainability-minded, zero pretension, with a serious tap-cocktail program and $4.50 old fashioneds. For October it is wearing a costume: the horror-themed Black Lagoon pop-up takes over the room all month, which suits the weekend before Halloween.<br>2151 S Kinnickinnic Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53207<br>Hours: Fri 4:00 PM - 2:30 AM · Sat 4:00 PM - 2:30 AM · Sun 12:00 PM - 10:00 PM · Mon 4:00 PM - 12:00 AM<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/lost-whale-milwaukee">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.lostwhalemke.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Lost+Whale+2151+S+Kinnickinnic+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9065,43.0054,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Boone &amp; Crockett</name><styleUrl>#s-bar</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[&#x27;Pretentious drinks without the pretentiousness&#x27;: a taxidermy-and-string-lights cocktail bar on the Kinnickinnic River in Walker&#x27;s Point, with a big waterfront patio, Taco Moto on site, and a 2 AM close every night it is open. The Trinidad Sour alone is worth the 25-minute riverwalk south.<br>818 S Water St, Milwaukee, WI 53204<br>Hours: Fri 3:00 PM - 2:00 AM · Sat 3:00 PM - 2:00 AM · Sun 3:00 PM - 2:00 AM · Mon Closed<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/boone-and-crockett-milwaukee">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.boonemilwaukee.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Boone+%26+Crockett+818+S+Water+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9066,43.0227,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Wolski&#x27;s Tavern</name><styleUrl>#s-bar</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A 1908 corner tavern on a residential street two blocks off Brady, run by the founder&#x27;s great-grandsons. Steel-tip darts, bar dice, a popcorn machine, Stoli Orange shots, cash only. Stay until last call and the bartender hands over the &#x27;I Closed Wolski&#x27;s&#x27; bumper sticker, which cannot be bought and has been spotted from Dublin to Osaka. I have never closed Wolski&#x27;s. The sticker gets around more than I do.<br>1836 N Pulaski St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri 2:00 PM - 2:30 AM · Sat 12:00 PM - 2:30 AM · Sun 12:00 PM - 2:00 AM · Mon 2:00 PM - 2:00 AM<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/wolskis-tavern-milwaukee">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.wolskis.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Wolski%27s+Tavern+1836+N+Pulaski+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.8966,43.0552,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Von Trier</name><styleUrl>#s-bar</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A dark, carved-wood German bierstube on the East Side (here since 1978, a tavern since Prohibition&#x27;s end) with 30 taps heavy on German imports, a Cyril Colnik chandelier rescued from the Pabst Mansion, hand-painted murals and a beer garden out back. When the city threatened to turn it into a sleek cocktail lounge in 2016, Milwaukee revolted and it stayed as it was.<br>2235 N Farwell Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri 3:00 PM - 2:30 AM · Sat 11:00 AM - 2:30 AM · Sun 11:00 AM - 12:00 AM · Mon 4:00 PM - 1:00 AM<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/von-trier-milwaukee">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.vontriers.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Von+Trier+2235+N+Farwell+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.886,43.0599,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Lost Whale (Black Lagoon pop-up)</name><styleUrl>#s-bar</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Bay View&#x27;s best cocktail bar in full horror-movie dress for October.<br>2151 S Kinnickinnic Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53207<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/lost-whale-milwaukee">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.lostwhalemke.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Lost+Whale+2151+S+Kinnickinnic+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9065,43.0054,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Eat</name>
<Placemark><name>Lakefront Brewery Beer Hall - Friday Night Fish Fry</name><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Friday in Milwaukee means fish fry, and this is the one with a live polka band in a riverside beer hall. Beer-battered cod, potato pancakes, a Riverwest Stein, and the Brewhaus Polka Kings from 5 to 8 PM, ten minutes from the Riverside.<br>1872 N Commerce St, Milwaukee, WI 53212<br>Hours: Fri 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM (fish fry kitchen 4:00 - 9:00 PM, table service) · Sat 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM · Sun 11:00 AM - 5:00 PM · Mon 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM (Beer Hall food 3:00 - 8:00 PM)<br>Order: Fish Fry Dinner: three-piece beer-battered cod with potato pancakes and applesauce ($20), Fried Walleye, hand-breaded, two pieces ($23), Cheese curds from the Cheese Curd Flavor of the Month board, A Riverwest Stein or Fixed Gear on draft, plus a brandy Old Fashioned sweet<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/lakefront-brewery-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://lakefrontbrewery.com/beer-hall">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Lakefront+Brewery+1872+N+Commerce+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9052,43.0547,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Three Brothers Serbian Restaurant</name><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A 1956 Serbian family restaurant inside an old Schlitz tiled-corner tavern in Bay View, run by the founder&#x27;s widow and daughters, and a James Beard America&#x27;s Classic (2002). The burek is baked to order and takes about half an hour, so it goes in first.<br>2414 S St Clair St, Milwaukee, WI 53207<br>Hours: Fri 5:00 - 9:00 PM · Sat 4:00 - 9:00 PM · Sun 4:00 - 9:00 PM · Mon Closed<br>Order: Burek (spinach and cheese, or meat), a giant baked phyllo pie, about 30 minutes to bake ($26.50), Chicken paprikash with potato dumplings, Roast lamb with house-pickled cabbage, Serbian salad and a glass of Serbian wine or slivovitz<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/three-brothers-restaurant-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.travelwisconsin.com/dining/three-brothers-restaurant-204614">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Three+Brothers+Restaurant+2414+S+St+Clair+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.8932,43.0003,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sanford Restaurant</name><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Milwaukee&#x27;s fine-dining standard since 1989, in the D&#x27;Amato family&#x27;s former corner grocery. A quiet 20-table room, polished service, and a seasonal four-course prix fixe. One dressed-up dinner this weekend belongs here.<br>1547 N Jackson St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri 5:30 - 10:00 PM · Sat 5:00 - 10:00 PM · Sun Closed · Mon Closed<br>Order: Four-course Prix Fixe ($105), the whole point, Surprise seven-course tasting menu ($135) only Tue-Fri, so Friday if time allows, Whatever the duck preparation is that night<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/sanford-restaurant-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.sanfordrestaurant.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Sanford+Restaurant+1547+N+Jackson+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.905,43.0505,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Odd Duck</name><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Walker&#x27;s Point&#x27;s playful, globally minded small-plates room, a regular on Milwaukee Magazine&#x27;s best-restaurants list. The menu changes constantly, the bar opens at 3:00 PM with a $7 spritz happy hour, and the kitchen fires at 5:00 PM, which is pre-show dinner timing.<br>939 S 2nd St, Milwaukee, WI 53204<br>Hours: Fri Bar 3:00 PM - 12:00 AM; kitchen 5:00 - 10:00 PM · Sat Bar 3:00 PM - 12:00 AM; kitchen 5:00 - 10:00 PM · Sun Closed (Tue-Sat only) · Mon Closed<br>Order: Ask for the current duck preparation (there is always one), Three or four shareable plates across the vegetable and seafood sections, Happy hour 3:00-6:00 PM at the bar: $7 spritz, $5 draft, $8 wine<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/odd-duck-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.oddduckrestaurant.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Odd+Duck+939+S+2nd+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9129,43.0213,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Birch</name><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Seasonal Midwestern cooking from a wood-fired hearth in a handsome room just north of downtown, with a 4:00-6:00 PM happy hour and a burger Milwaukee Magazine calls top-tier. Dinner starts at 5:00 PM Friday and Saturday.<br>459 E Pleasant St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri Happy hour 4:00 - 6:00 PM; dinner 5:00 - 10:00 PM · Sat 5:00 - 10:00 PM · Sun Closed (not listed; Tue-Sat only) · Mon Closed<br>Order: Anything from the hearth: the whole roasted fish or the wood-fired pork, The Birch burger (a Milwaukee Magazine top pick), Happy hour 4:00-6:00 PM Friday at the bar before dinner<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/birch-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.birchonpleasant.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Birch+459+E+Pleasant+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9068,43.0509,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mader&#x27;s Restaurant</name><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Milwaukee&#x27;s 120-year-old German landmark on Old World Third Street: suits of armor, stained glass, a Hofbrau pour, and a pork shank that calls for a nap. Ten minutes on foot from the Riverside, and open Sunday and Monday when much of the city is dark.<br>1041 N Old World 3rd St, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br>Hours: Fri 11:30 AM - 10:00 PM · Sat 11:30 AM - 10:00 PM · Sun 11:30 AM - 8:00 PM · Mon 11:30 AM - 9:00 PM<br>Order: Bavarian Platter (schnitzel, kassler, bratwurst, sauerkraut, spaetzle), Wiener Schnitzel, Roasted pork shank, A brandy Old Fashioned sweet, the Wisconsin way, or a liter of Hofbrau<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/maders-milwaukee-3?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.madersrestaurant.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Mader&#x27;s+Restaurant+1041+N+Old+World+3rd+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9149,43.0439,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Solly&#x27;s Grille</name><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Home of the butter burger since 1936 and a James Beard America&#x27;s Classic (2022): a horseshoe lunch counter where the patty is steamed in butter and then topped with a melting slab of more butter. A real malt goes with it. Lunch only, closed Sunday and Monday, so Friday or Saturday.<br>4629 N Port Washington Rd, Glendale, WI 53212<br>Hours: Fri 7:00 AM - 7:00 PM · Sat 7:00 AM - 7:00 PM · Sun Closed · Mon Closed<br>Order: The Original Butter Burger (ask for grilled onions), A chocolate malt or shake, Fries<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/sollys-grille-glendale?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solly%27s_Grille">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Solly&#x27;s+Grille+4629+N+Port+Washington+Rd+Glendale">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9174,43.1003,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>La Dama</name><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Chef Emmanuel Corona&#x27;s mural-walled Mexican kitchen in Walker&#x27;s Point, the South Side&#x27;s old Mexican heart. Mole poblano and mole negro from his childhood, a deep mezcal list, and a 4:30 PM Sunday opening that fits the early-dinner window exactly.<br>839 S 2nd St, Milwaukee, WI 53204<br>Hours: Fri 5:00 - 9:30 PM · Sat 5:00 - 9:30 PM · Sun 4:30 - 8:00 PM · Mon Closed<br>Order: Mole poblano or mole negro (the house signatures), Octopus, A mezcal flight or a mezcal cocktail, Churros or the dessert of the night<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/la-dama-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.ladamamke.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=La+Dama+839+S+2nd+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9129,43.0223,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Uncle Wolfie&#x27;s Breakfast Tavern (Downtown)</name><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Milwaukee&#x27;s favorite breakfast tavern, now with a downtown room eight minutes&#x27; walk from the Riverside. Walk-in only, open 8:00 AM to 2:00 PM Monday, and the Monday crowd is a fraction of the weekend line.<br>600 N Broadway, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri 8:00 AM - 2:00 PM (The Wolf dinner 5:00 - 10:00 PM) · Sat 8:00 AM - 3:00 PM (The Wolf dinner 5:00 - 10:00 PM) · Sun 8:00 AM - 3:00 PM · Mon 8:00 AM - 2:00 PM<br>Order: The breakfast sandwich or any egg plate with the house potatoes, A Bloody Mary (it is a breakfast tavern) or the coffee cocktail, Whatever pastry is on the counter<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/uncle-wolfies-downtown-and-the-wolf-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.unclewolfies.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Uncle+Wolfie&#x27;s+600+N+Broadway+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9075,43.0376,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Honeypie Cafe</name><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Bay View&#x27;s Midwestern-comfort cafe with house-baked pies the critics line up for, buttermilk biscuits, and house-infused Bloody Marys. It sits on Kinnickinnic Avenue, on the way to the airport (10 minutes from MKE), and it is open Monday from 9:00 AM.<br>2569 S Kinnickinnic Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53207<br>Hours: Fri 9:00 AM - 3:00 PM breakfast/lunch; 3:00 - 9:00 PM dinner · Sat 9:00 AM - 3:00 PM brunch; 3:00 - 9:00 PM dinner · Sun 9:00 AM - 3:00 PM brunch; 3:00 - 9:00 PM dinner · Mon 9:00 AM - 3:00 PM breakfast/lunch; 3:00 - 9:00 PM dinner<br>Order: A slice of pie (ask what came out of the oven; take a second slice to go), Buttermilk biscuits and gravy, House-infused Bloody Mary with a beer chaser<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/honeypie-cafe-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.honeypiecafe.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Honeypie+Cafe+2569+S+Kinnickinnic+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9004,42.998,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sobelman&#x27;s Pub &amp; Grill (original, St. Paul Ave)</name><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The 1890s Schlitz tavern in the Menomonee Valley that made Milwaukee&#x27;s over-garnished Bloody Mary famous (bacon-wrapped cheddar balls, sausage, a beer chaser), backed by a top-tier burger. Opens 11:00 AM Monday, a late Monday brunch disguised as lunch, and I-94 to the airport is right there.<br>1900 W St Paul Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53233<br>Hours: Fri 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM · Sat 10:00 AM - 9:00 PM · Sun Closed · Mon 11:00 AM - 8:00 PM<br>Order: The Bloody Masterpiece (or the Baconado) with the beer chaser, The Sobelman burger (or the Beast), Bacon-wrapped jalapeno cheeseballs<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/sobelmans-pub-and-grill-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.sobelmanspubandgrill.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Sobelman&#x27;s+Pub+and+Grill+1900+W+St+Paul+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9368,43.0349,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kopp&#x27;s Frozen Custard (Greenfield, on the way to MKE)</name><styleUrl>#s-restaurant</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Milwaukee&#x27;s custard temple: a stainless-steel stand on Layton Avenue, the road that runs straight east to the airport. Two Flavors of the Day on a chalkboard and jumbo butter burgers. Monday Oct 26 flavors are Twix-Tac-Dough and Cookies &#x27;N Cream.<br>7631 W Layton Ave, Greenfield, WI 53220<br>Hours: Fri 10:30 AM - 11:00 PM · Sat 10:30 AM - 11:00 PM · Sun 10:30 AM - 10:00 PM · Mon 10:30 AM - 10:00 PM<br>Order: A dish of the Flavor of the Day (Monday: Twix-Tac-Dough or Cookies &#x27;N Cream), Jumbo butter burger with fried onions, Caramel Apple Sundae (October sundae of the month)<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/kopps-frozen-custard-greenfield-3?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.kopps.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Kopp&#x27;s+Frozen+Custard+7631+W+Layton+Ave+Greenfield">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-88.0093,42.9586,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Street food</name>
<Placemark><name>3rd Street Market Hall</name><styleUrl>#s-street-food</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A food hall with twenty-plus stalls and a bar two blocks west of the Riverside, on the same side of Wisconsin Avenue. Lao food at SapSap, Cambodian sandwiches at Num Pang, Wisconsin cheese curds and mac at Rod-N-Makk, tacos at Kompali, Pizza Shuttle slices, Bebe Zito ice cream. Open until 10:00 PM Fri/Sat, so it is the pre-show grazing hall.<br>275 W Wisconsin Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br>Hours: Fri Food hall 8:00 AM - 10:00 PM; bar 11:00 AM - 11:00 PM · Sat Food hall 9:00 AM - 10:00 PM; bar 11:00 AM - 11:00 PM · Sun Food hall 9:00 AM - 7:00 PM; bar 11:00 AM - 7:00 PM · Mon Food hall 8:00 AM - 8:00 PM; bar 11:00 AM - 9:00 PM<br>Order: SapSap: Lao sausage or khao poon, Rod-N-Makk: Wisconsin cheese curds and a mac bowl, Num Pang: Cambodian sandwich on house baguette, Mr. Dye&#x27;s Pies: a slice for the walk to the show<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/3rd-street-market-hall-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://3rdstmarkethall.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=3rd+Street+Market+Hall+275+W+Wisconsin+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9147,43.0383,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Milwaukee Public Market</name><styleUrl>#s-street-food</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The Third Ward&#x27;s market hall: St. Paul Fish Company&#x27;s lobster rolls and oysters at the palapa bar, West Allis Cheese &amp; Sausage&#x27;s curds, C. Adam&#x27;s cakes, Thief Wine&#x27;s bar upstairs, Anodyne coffee. A ten-minute walk from the Riverside and the best late-breakfast-into-lunch stroll downtown.<br>400 N Water St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri 10:00 AM - 8:00 PM · Sat 10:00 AM - 8:00 PM · Sun 10:00 AM - 6:00 PM · Mon 10:00 AM - 8:00 PM<br>Order: St. Paul Fish Company: lobster roll, chowder, or oysters at the palapa bar with a Bloody Mary, West Allis Cheese &amp; Sausage Shoppe: fresh cheese curds and a Usinger-style sausage sampler, C. Adam&#x27;s Bakery: a kringle slice or cake, Thief Wine: a glass on the mezzanine<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/milwaukee-public-market-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://milwaukeepublicmarket.org/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Milwaukee+Public+Market+400+N+Water+St">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9076,43.0352,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Real Chili (Downtown)</name><styleUrl>#s-street-food</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Milwaukee&#x27;s post-bar ritual since 1931: a counter, a bowl of chili ladled over spaghetti and beans, mild to hot, a fistful of oyster crackers, and a dash of hot vinegar. Open until 3:00 AM Friday and Saturday, ten minutes&#x27; walk from the theater.<br>419 E Wells St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri 11:00 AM - 3:00 AM · Sat 11:00 AM - 3:00 AM · Sun Closed (Marquette location at 1625 W Wells open 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM) · Mon 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM<br>Order: Marquette Special: chili over spaghetti with beans, medium heat, Chili cheese dog, Oyster crackers and the hot vinegar shaker on the counter, A cold Miller High Life<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/real-chili-restaurant-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.realchilimilwaukee.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Real+Chili+419+E+Wells+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9059,43.0411,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ian&#x27;s Pizza Downtown (Cream City Arcade)</name><styleUrl>#s-street-food</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Wisconsin&#x27;s cult by-the-slice shop (born in Madison), with a downtown location that doubles as an arcade, open until 2:00 AM Friday and Saturday. The Mac n&#x27; Cheese slice is the thing. A 14-minute walk north of the Riverside, or a 4-minute ride.<br>146 E Juneau Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri 11:00 AM - 2:00 AM · Sat 11:00 AM - 2:00 AM · Sun 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM · Mon 11:00 AM - 10:00 PM<br>Order: Signature Mac n&#x27; Cheese slice, Whatever the rotating specialty slice is (often a Wisconsin-themed one), Garlic butter and ranch on the side, the local way<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/ians-pizza-milwaukee-milwaukee-2?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://ianspizza.com/location/ians-pizza-cream-city-milwaukee/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Ian&#x27;s+Pizza+146+E+Juneau+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9116,43.0459,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Milwaukee Brat House (Downtown)</name><styleUrl>#s-street-food</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A beer-and-brats tavern on Old World Third, next door to Mader&#x27;s and a 9-minute walk from the venue. Brats with kraut, fried cheese curds, pretzels, and a bar open until 2:00 AM every night including Sunday, which makes it the late-night Milwaukee cliche after the Sunday show.<br>1013 N Old World 3rd St, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br>Hours: Fri 11:00 AM - 2:00 AM · Sat 10:00 AM - 2:30 AM · Sun 10:00 AM - 2:00 AM · Mon 11:00 AM - 2:00 AM<br>Order: Classic bratwurst with sauerkraut and stadium mustard, Fried Wisconsin cheese curds, A local draft (Lakefront, New Glarus Spotted Cow if they have it)<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/milwaukee-brat-house-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://www.milwaukeebrathouse.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Milwaukee+Brat+House+1013+N+Old+World+3rd+St">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9148,43.0433,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Pizza Shuttle</name><styleUrl>#s-street-food</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The East Side&#x27;s 40-year late-night institution: takeout and delivery until 3:00 AM every night, including Sunday, with a dine-in room until midnight. Pizza, broasted chicken, gyros, wonton mozzarella sticks, and a strawberry custard shake. The Sunday-night safety net that delivers to a downtown hotel.<br>1827 N Farwell Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br>Hours: Fri Dine-in 10:00 AM - 12:00 AM; takeout/delivery 10:00 AM - 3:00 AM · Sat Dine-in 10:00 AM - 12:00 AM; takeout/delivery 10:00 AM - 3:00 AM · Sun Dine-in 10:00 AM - 12:00 AM; takeout/delivery 10:00 AM - 3:00 AM · Mon Dine-in 10:00 AM - 12:00 AM; takeout/delivery 10:00 AM - 3:00 AM<br>Order: A slice or small pie (the Deluxe), Broasted chicken, Wonton mozzarella sticks, Strawberry shake made with fresh custard<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/pizza-shuttle-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://pizzashuttle.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Pizza+Shuttle+1827+N+Farwell+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.8911,43.0547,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>See</name>
<Placemark><name>Riverside Theater</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A 2,480-seat 1928 vaudeville-and-movie palace by Kirchhoff &amp; Rose, tucked under the 12-story Empire Building that RKO built. Panic has played it since 2006 and done three-night fall stands here most years since 2008. Locals treat the run like a holiday.<br>116 W Wisconsin Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br><a href="https://www.pabsttheatergroup.com/events/venue/the-riverside-theater">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Riverside+Theater+116+W+Wisconsin+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9109,43.0389,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Gertie the Duck statue</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[In April 1945 a mallard nested on a piling under this bridge and a war-weary country followed her ducklings in the newspaper. Gwendolyn Gillen&#x27;s bronze Gertie and her brood have sat on the bridge since 1997, about 150 feet from the Riverside marquee.<br>Wisconsin Avenue Bridge (northwest corner), Milwaukee, WI 53203<br><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gertie_the_Duck">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Gertie+the+Duck+Wisconsin+Avenue+Bridge+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9102,43.0388,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Bronze Fonz</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Henry Winkler&#x27;s Fonzie in bronze, double thumbs up, unveiled in 2008 with most of the Happy Days cast present. Two blocks from the theater on the Riverwalk. The obligatory Milwaukee selfie.<br>Milwaukee RiverWalk, just south of E Wells St (east bank), Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze_Fonz">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Bronze+Fonz+Milwaukee+Riverwalk">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.911,43.0404,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Usinger&#x27;s Famous Sausage</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Sausage-makers since 1880, in a shop with hand-painted elf murals, directly across from Mader&#x27;s. A snack-size bratwurst or summer sausage travels well to a hotel room, and they ship.<br>1030 N Old World 3rd St (N Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Dr), Milwaukee, WI 53203<br><a href="https://www.usinger.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Usinger%27s+Famous+Sausage+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.914,43.0437,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>St. James 1868</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A deconsecrated 1868 Episcopal church turned event space, 10 minutes west on Wisconsin Avenue. On Sunday Oct 25 it hosts &#x27;Candlelight: A Haunted Evening of Halloween Classics&#x27; at 4:30 PM and 6:45 PM. The 4:30 show ends in time for the 6:30 doors.<br>833 W Wisconsin Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53233<br><a href="https://onmilwaukee.com/articles/halloween-2026">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=St.+James+1868+833+W+Wisconsin+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9231,43.0382,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Milwaukee City Hall</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The 1895 Flemish Renaissance tower that was briefly among the tallest buildings in America, and the one in the Laverne &amp; Shirley opening credits. The lobby in daytime is worth the detour: an eight-story open atrium ringed with iron railings, one of the great civic interiors in the Midwest.<br>200 E Wells St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://city.milwaukee.gov/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Milwaukee+City+Hall+200+E+Wells+St">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9098,43.0417,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Pabst Theater</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Captain Frederick Pabst&#x27;s 1895 opera house, sister venue to the Riverside, and the meeting point for the &#x27;Shadow of City Hall&#x27; ghost walk (select Fri/Sat 7:30 PM, $33.57, ~2 hours, covering the Pfister ghost, City Hall and the Newhall House fire site).<br>144 E Wells St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://www.pabsttheatergroup.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Pabst+Theater+144+E+Wells+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9105,43.0411,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Milwaukee Art Museum (Quadracci Pavilion)</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Santiago Calatrava&#x27;s 2001 pavilion with the Burke Brise Soleil, a 217-foot pair of wings that open in the morning and fold at night (and close automatically if wind tops 23 mph). Friday Oct 23, 7-11 PM, is &#x27;MAM After Dark: Halloween Bash&#x27; ($35 advance / $40 door) with a dress-as-an-artwork costume contest. It collides with the show, and it explains the costumes on the lakefront.<br>700 N Art Museum Dr, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://mam.org/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Milwaukee+Art+Museum+700+N+Art+Museum+Dr">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.8971,43.0398,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Brothers Bar &amp; Grill (Boos Fest Halloween Crawl check-in)</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Starting point for the Saturday Oct 24 &#x27;Boos Fest&#x27; Halloween bar crawl (doors 6 PM, late check-in by 8 PM, GA $24.99 advance / $40 door) that works through Water Street and Old World Third. A college-crowd crawl, not a quality-bar crawl, but the costumes on Water Street Saturday night will be a show of their own.<br>1213 N Water St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://www.barcrawlnation.com/events/milwaukee-boos-fest-halloween-crawl-2026">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Brothers+Bar+%26+Grill+1213+N+Water+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9115,43.0461,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Catalano Square (World Series block party screens)</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Fri Oct 23 and Sat Oct 24, noon-11 PM: Third Ward Beer Garden and the Historic Third Ward Association close Menomonee Street for food trucks, big screens showing Games 1 and 2, Brewers cocktails, and live tapings of the Foul Territory podcast 5-7 PM. The city&#x27;s first World Series in 44 years, so the pregame energy around 5 PM will be something.<br>Menomonee St &amp; N Broadway, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://www.milwaukeemag.com/watch-the-brewers-in-the-world-series-at-this-block-party/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Catalano+Square+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9068,43.0311,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Pearl &amp; Cade (The Nightmare Bar pop-up)</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Fever&#x27;s ticketed horror-themed pop-up bar in the Phoenix Building, Oct 8-31: 90-minute sessions at 7 PM and 9 PM, 21+, $17.50 with a welcome drink, costumes encouraged. Both sessions overlap the show, so it is a Monday-afternoon curiosity at most, barring a skipped set break.<br>219 N Milwaukee St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://feverup.com/m/737479">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Pearl+%26+Cade+219+N+Milwaukee+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9062,43.0333,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Outsider (Kimpton Journeyman rooftop)</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Ninth-floor rooftop bar over the Third Ward with fire pits and a skyline view. A golden-hour stop (sunset is about 5:55 PM) before the 12-minute walk north to the street party. Hours not verified for this weekend, so check before going.<br>310 E Chicago St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://www.journeymanhotel.com/the-outsider">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=The+Outsider+Rooftop+310+E+Chicago+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9068,43.033,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Fiserv Forum</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Home of the Bucks, with a swooping zinc roof. The Bucks moved their home-opener tipoff this week so it would not collide with the Brewers&#x27; World Series run. That is how much this city is living baseball right now.<br>1111 Vel R. Phillips Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53203<br><a href="https://www.fiservforum.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Fiserv+Forum+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9175,43.045,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Glorioso&#x27;s Italian Market</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Family-run Italian grocery and deli since 1946, the anchor of Brady Street. The Italian sub and the cannoli are the move for a Saturday or Sunday lunch before a stroll.<br>1011 E Brady St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://www.gloriosos.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Glorioso%27s+Italian+Market+1011+E+Brady+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.8993,43.0528,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Landmark Lanes</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A subterranean 1927 bowling alley under the Oriental Theatre with three bars, a retro arcade, pool and darts. 21+ after 9 PM, bar open until 2 AM nightly, bowling until 11 PM. Directly across from Von Trier.<br>2220 N Farwell Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://www.landmarklanes.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Landmark+Lanes+2220+N+Farwell+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.8857,43.0597,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Lakefront Brewery</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The most fun brewery tour in America, in an old riverside power plant across the river from Brady Street: 50 minutes, four 8-oz pours, a souvenir pint glass and a free-beer coupon good at local bars, $16 Fri-Sun. The beer hall has a Friday fish fry and Bernie Brewer&#x27;s original chalet from County Stadium. Tours run roughly hourly Sat noon-6 PM, Sun noon and 2 PM. The beer hall closes 9 PM (5 PM Sunday).<br>1872 N Commerce St, Milwaukee, WI 53212<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/lakefront-brewery-milwaukee">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://lakefrontbrewery.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Lakefront+Brewery+1872+N+Commerce+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9052,43.0547,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Allen-Bradley Clock Tower (the &#x27;Polish Moon&#x27;)</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Dedicated on Halloween 1962, with four faces more than 40 feet across. It was the largest four-faced clock in the world until Mecca&#x27;s Abraj Al Bait topped it. South-siders call the glowing faces the Polish Moon. Visible from Blu&#x27;s windows and from most of Walker&#x27;s Point.<br>1201 S 2nd St, Milwaukee, WI 53204<br><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockwell_Automation_Headquarters_and_Allen-Bradley_Clock_Tower">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Allen-Bradley+Clock+Tower+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9147,43.0178,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Harley-Davidson Museum</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Twenty acres on the Menomonee River telling the story that began in a 10-by-15-foot Davidson-family shed in 1903. Non-riders go for the Engine Room and the &#x27;tsunami bike&#x27; that washed up in Canada. A 15-minute walk from the Riverside, and the MOTOR bar and restaurant does a solid lunch.<br>400 W Canal St, Milwaukee, WI 53201<br><a href="https://www.harley-davidson.com/us/en/museum.html">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Harley-Davidson+Museum+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.917,43.0313,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Basilica of St. Josaphat</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Polish immigrants built this 1901 basilica, dome 214 feet high, out of the demolished Chicago federal post office, which their pastor bought for $20,000 and shipped north on 500 railroad flatcars. Ten minutes south of Bryant&#x27;s by car, an easy pairing with cocktails there.<br>2333 S 6th St, Milwaukee, WI 53215<br><a href="https://thebasilica.org/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Basilica+of+St.+Josaphat+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9192,43.0025,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Burnhearts</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A Bay View corner bar with a serious craft-beer list and a pinball corner, named &#x27;my favorite bar in Milwaukee&#x27; in the 2015 Panic fan guide. Two blocks from At Random. Hours not verified for this weekend.<br>2599 S Logan Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53207<br><a href="https://www.burnhearts.com/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Burnhearts+2599+S+Logan+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.897,42.9973,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Holler House</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A 1908 tavern whose two basement lanes are the oldest sanctioned tenpin lanes in the United States, still set by human pinsetters. Hundreds of signed bras hang from the ceiling, a tradition the late owner Marcy Skowronski started one rowdy night. Call ahead for lane time, and cash is wise.<br>2042 W Lincoln Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53215<br><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holler_House">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Holler+House+2042+W+Lincoln+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9396,43.0032,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Walgreens (24-hour store), Brady &amp; Farwell</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Open 24 hours for Advil, water, snacks and phone chargers. Pharmacy counter 8 AM. Phone 414-272-2171. About a 7-minute rideshare from the hotel.<br>1400 E Brady St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://www.walgreens.com/locator/walgreens-1400+e+brady+st-milwaukee-wi-53202/id=1685">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Walgreens+1400+E+Brady+St+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.8935,43.0531,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Aurora Urgent Care, Schlitz Park</name><styleUrl>#s-landmark</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Walk-in urgent care in the old Schlitz brewery complex. Weekend hours 8 AM - 4 PM per directory listing. Confirm by phone, 414-276-4242.<br>1575 N RiverCenter Dr, Milwaukee, WI 53212<br><a href="https://www.aurorahealthcare.org/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Aurora+Urgent+Care+1575+N+RiverCenter+Dr+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9098,43.0514,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Laverne &amp; Shirley</name>
<Placemark><name>Milwaukee County Historical Society</name><styleUrl>#s-laverne</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The 1913 bank building on Pere Marquette Park is where the actual &#x27;Welcome Milwaukee Visitors&#x27; letters from the opening credits ended up (City Hall gave them to the art school MIAD, which handed them here in 2012). Staff spelled PENNY in the river windows when Marshall died and CINDY when Williams did. Cheap, quick, and a real piece of the show to stand next to. Ask at the desk whether the letters are out.<br>910 N Dr Martin Luther King Jr Dr (Old World Third St), Milwaukee, WI 53203<br><a href="https://milwaukeehistory.net/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Milwaukee+County+Historical+Society+910+N+Dr+Martin+Luther+King+Jr+Dr">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9142,43.0419,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Best Place at the Historic Pabst Brewery</name><styleUrl>#s-laverne</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Shotz never existed, but this did: the 1800s Pabst brewery complex, the cream-city-brick beer castle the show was pretending to be. The hour-long Beer History Tour ($14, includes a pint) walks through Captain Pabst&#x27;s old offices and reception hall, and the Blue Ribbon Hall tavern pours Pabst, Schlitz, and Blatz under a mural ceiling. For these dates: Haunted Pabst Brewery flashlight tours run Sunday Oct 25 and Monday Oct 26 at 6:00 and 7:30 PM ($20, includes a tallboy).<br>917 W Juneau Ave, Milwaukee, WI 53233<br><a href="https://www.yelp.com/biz_photos/best-place-at-the-historic-pabst-brewery-milwaukee?tab=food">Yelp food photos</a><br><a href="https://bestplacemilwaukee.com/tours/">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Best+Place+at+the+Historic+Pabst+Brewery+917+W+Juneau+Ave+Milwaukee">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9234,43.0455,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Milwaukee Public Museum: Streets of Old Milwaukee</name><styleUrl>#s-laverne</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[A walk-through, lamp-lit replica of turn-of-the-century Milwaukee streets (cobblestones, a candy shop, Grandma peering out her window) that has been a rite of passage for every Milwaukee kid since 1965. It is the closest thing to a Shotz-era streetscape anyone can stroll, and this is the last chance: the Wells Street museum closes for good January 3, 2027, before moving to the new Nature &amp; Culture Museum. Right now it is dressed for &#x27;Historic Halloween&#x27; through November 1.<br>800 W Wells St, Milwaukee, WI 53233<br><a href="https://www.mpm.edu/plan-visit">Website</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Milwaukee+Public+Museum+800+W+Wells+St">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.9213,43.0407,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>730 E Knapp Street (Laverne &amp; Shirley&#x27;s address)</name><styleUrl>#s-laverne</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The girls gave their address as 730 Knapp Street, and Knapp Street is real: a quiet lower-east-side block of row houses and condos about a 12-minute walk northeast of the Riverside. There is no plaque, no basement apartment, and nothing was filmed here, which is the point. Take the photo under the street sign, caption it &#x27;Shirley, we&#x27;re home,&#x27; and move on.<br>730 E Knapp St, Milwaukee, WI 53202<br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=730+E+Knapp+St+Milwaukee+WI">Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-87.903,43.047,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
</Document></kml>